    <bpmn:process id="W_W5542" name="W5542. Liquidity Stress, Covenant-Breach &amp; Payment-Prioritization Escalation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: The 13-week rolling cash forecast breaches the minimum-liquidity floor (days-of-cover floor per the W3400 working-capital policy); W319 covenant monitoring signals headroom &lt; 10% or an actual breach; or a funding-impairment event (W5541 bank failure, W3382 SCF facility suspension) puts the disbursement calendar at risk
Frequency: Rare; 0–2 stress declarations per year expected (seasonal build + a funding shock is the classic compound scenario)
Volume: 1 declaration × the full enterprise disbursement calendar (~PHP 5B/month receipts cycle per the W1474 canon) × all funding facilities (revolving credit, W3377 SCF program, W170-class pledge lines) × ~5,200 trade vendors&#x27; payment terms
Owner: CFO
Participants: Treasury Manager (cash council chair), Finance Controller, VP Merchandising (inventory levers per W3395), AR/Credit Manager (DSO levers per W3396), AP Manager (payment execution per W556), Procurement Director (vendor terms), SCF Program Lead (facility drawdown per W3377/W3382), VP Legal (waiver/cure documentation), Internal Audit (observer), Board/Audit Committee, lenders
Source: workflow W5542 — Liquidity Stress, Covenant-Breach &amp; Payment-Prioritization Escalation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5542_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5542_Lane1" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5542_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5542_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5542_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5542_Lane2" name="Treasury">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5542_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5542_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5542_Lane3" name="Cash council members">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5542_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5542_Lane4" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5542_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5542_Lane5" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5542_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5542_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5542_Start7" name="The 13-week rolling cash forecast breaches the minimum-liquidity floor (days-of-cover…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5542_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5542_Task8" name="Stress declaration &amp; cash council">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Stress declaration &amp; cash council: CFO declares stress on the trigger evidence (floor breach, covenant headroom, funding impairment); daily cash council stands up (Treasury chair, Controller, AP, AR/Credit, Procurement, SCF Lead); 13-week forecast re-locked daily with weekly-versus-baseline variance; declaration logged with trigger evidence
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Day 0–1</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5542_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5542_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5542_Task9" name="Root-cause &amp; horizon classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Root-cause &amp; horizon classification: seasonal (ber-months inventory build vs structural) — seasonal stress borrows against the post-season ramp; structural (margin/composition decay) or event-driven (W5541-class impairment, facility suspension) — class sets which levers are on the table and the exit criteria
Responsible (R): Treasury / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Day 1–2</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5542_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5542_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5542_Task10" name="Lever sequence (reversibility-ordered)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Lever sequence (reversibility-ordered): (a) accelerate collections — DSO sprint per W3396 (collection-cadence surge on top-200 AR accounts, credit-hold discipline per W68); (b) draw available committed liquidity — revolving facility, W3382 SCF utilization headroom; (c) stretch payables *within terms* — W3394 DPO levers, negotiated short extensions with critical vendors; (d) release valves — W3395 inventory cash-release (OTB freeze on discretionary buys per W101), W21-class capex deferral gate; (e) last-rung — non-core asset disposals. Each lever has an owner, an expected PHP range, and a decision deadline
Responsible (R): Cash council members
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Day 2–10</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5542_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5542_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5542_Task11" name="Payment prioritization tiers (when cash &lt; obligations)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payment prioritization tiers (when cash &lt; obligations): Tier 1 — statutory wages &amp; government remittances (payroll per W10/W5540, SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG/BIR per W1527/W1306); Tier 2 — secured/pledged obligations &amp; LC settlements (W170/W1455 classes — collateral at risk), payroll funding accounts; Tier 3 — critical-supply and SCF-settled vendors (program-exit risk per W3384); Tier 4 — remaining trade payables by criticality and cost-of-default; the AP run executes the tiers, and exceptions require CFO sign-off
Responsible (R): Treasury / AP Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Ongoing under stress</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5542_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5542_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5542_Task12" name="Covenant management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Covenant management: on breach or headroom &lt; 10% — VP Legal + Treasury open lender engagement (waiver request, cure plan, equity/asset-cure options per the W319 facility terms); no covenant notice is ever allowed to lapse silently; covenant-compliance certificate calendar enforced
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per facility terms</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5542_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5542_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5542_Task13" name="Governance clock &amp; communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Governance clock &amp; communication: Audit Committee/Board notified within 5 business days of declaration (and immediately on actual breach); lender disclosures per facility covenants; no selective disclosure per the W5017 canon if material; employee/customer-facing messaging only via approved comms (W855 discipline)
Responsible (R): CFO / VP Legal
Accountable (A): Board/Audit Committee
Duration: Day 5 + ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5542_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5542_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5542_Task14" name="Exit, floor recalibration &amp; post-mortem">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Exit, floor recalibration &amp; post-mortem: declare exit when 13-week forecast holds the floor + buffer for 4 consecutive weeks; post-mortem — trigger timing, lever effectiveness vs claimed ranges, KRI threshold recalibration in the VS-21.2 risk register (early-warning lead time), working-capital floor and covenant-headroom policy updates per W3400
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5542_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5542_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5542_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5542_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-546 (ensure controlled execution — Working Capital Analytics &amp; Cash-Conversion-Cycle Governance (PA-105.3).); CTL-61 (ensure debt covenant monitoring.) | - operational: statutory wages and government remittances are Tier-1 under any prioritization; tier exceptions require CFO sign-off with logged rationale | - operational: declaration and exit decisions carry documented trigger evidence against the W3400 policy floor
Owner: CFO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5542_Assoc17" sourceRef="W5542_Annotation16" targetRef="W5542_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
